{
  "id": "Compound::DB01223 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Aminophylline is shown to interact with multiple cytochrome P450 enzymes, specifically Cyp1a2 and Cyp2e1, through binding interactions. These enzymes are involved in metabolic processes that involve oxidation, including the oxidation of quinones and fatty acids. The shared participation of Cyp3a4 in these metabolic pathways suggests a potential link between Aminophylline and Cyp3a4. The evidence indicates that Aminophylline may influence Cyp3a4 through its effects on other enzymes, which in turn modulate Cyp3a4's activity. This mechanism is supported by the observed participation of Cyp3a4 in oxidation reactions, suggesting that Aminophylline could indirectly affect Cyp3a4 by altering the metabolic environment or by influencing the activity of other enzymes that are part of the same pathway. The integration of these findings highlights a possible role for Aminophylline in modulating Cyp3a4 activity through a network of metabolic interactions.",
